<application>
  <!-- Appearance > Accessibility > Zoom.

       A FALLBACK FOR AN UNATTENDED SESSION, and nothing more. Native resolution
       (enable_hidpi, seeded in kasmvnc-subpath-fix.html) renders at the device's
       real pixels, which is sharper and correspondingly smaller, so the IDE must
       be scaled by the client's devicePixelRatio to come out at the right
       physical size — and THIS IS NOT THE OPTION THAT DOES THAT.

       Zoom scales TEXT ONLY. Measured by screenshotting a live IDE at 200%:
       fonts grew while the toolbar, icons, tree rows, dialogs and status bar
       stayed exactly where they were, which reads as a broken IDE rather than a
       large one. The setting that moves the whole UI is the JVM's own
       -Dsun.java2d.uiScale, which the workspace sets from the reported ratio;
       when it does, it also pins THIS value to 1, because the two compound and
       a DPR-2 session would otherwise render at 2 x 1.25.

       So 1.25 is what a session gets only when no ratio is ever reported — a
       headless start, or a deployment with no listener — which is the behaviour
       this file had before reporting existed. A developer who sets their own
       Zoom keeps it: the workspace records what it wrote and never overwrites a
       value it did not leave behind.

       NotRoamableUiSettings/ideScale is what the Settings UI actually reads and
       writes — verified by changing the setting in a live IDE and finding it
       here. `-Dide.ui.scale` (also set, in the entrypoint's vmoptions) does NOT
       back this control in ASfP 2025.3; it was the obvious-looking lever and it
       left Settings > Zoom untouched at 100%. "Not roamable" is correct for a
       scale: it is a property of the display this session is streamed to. -->
  <component name="NotRoamableUiSettings">
    <option name="ideScale" value="1.25" />
  </component>
</application>
